<header><p class="st-kicker">chiefdom · France and the Low Countries</p><h1 class="st-title">Sotiates</h1><p class="st-meta">300 BCE – 56 BCE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Aquitanian people of the Sos district whose king Adiatuanus made a last stand against Rome with six hundred sworn companions.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Sotiates were one of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aquitani">Aquitani</a>, living around the oppidum of Sos in the modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lot-et-garonne">Lot-et-Garonne</a>, north of the Pyrenean foothills. They are known almost entirely from Caesar's account of the campaign of his legate <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/publius-licinius-crassus">Publius Crassus</a> in 56 BCE.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Caesar describes their king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adiatuanus">Adiatuanus</a> surrounded by six hundred soldurii, sworn companions who vowed to share their lord's fate and never survive him. Coins inscribed with the names of the Sotiates and of Adiatuanus confirm the account.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marcus-licinius-crassus">Crassus</a> defeated the Sotiates in open battle and besieged their oppidum; the defenders, skilled from their <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/copper">copper</a> mines, tried in vain to undermine the Roman siege works. After a failed sortie <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adiatuanus">Adiatuanus</a> surrendered. Their land later formed part of the Roman province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gallia-aquitania">Aquitania</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/sotiates.jpg" alt="Sotiates" width="320" height="274"><figcaption>Image: Sémhur · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aquitani_tribes_map-fr.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>300 BCE – 56 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>chiefdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Adiatuanus</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Aquitanian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/france">France</a></dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-178&amp;focus=sotiates" aria-label="Sotiates on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4766 550 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Sotiates lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5304 942h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5086 806h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5086 806h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day France. <a href="/atlas?year=-178&amp;focus=sotiates">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

